<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Android 12+ (API 31) draws the launch screen itself through the platform
      SplashScreen API and ignores `windowBackground`, so the branded launch has
      to be declared again in its own vocabulary or these devices fall back to
      the system default.

      The icon has to be declared too, and this is the part that took two
      attempts. Left to itself, the platform centres `@mipmap/ic_launcher` —
      legacy square bitmaps, no `mipmap-anydpi-v26` adaptive icon — and applies
      its legacy-icon treatment, which bakes a white circular backdrop into the
      icon drawable and shrinks the mark inside it. On Bufón's butter field that
      read as a white ring around a butter square around a tiny jester.

      `windowSplashScreenIconBackgroundColor` does NOT fix that, and was
      measured proving it: the baked white circle paints *over* the theme's
      icon-background colour, so the attribute is completely inert here. Do not
      re-add it.

      Naming `splash_isotype` as the splash icon does fix it. The platform fits
      the drawable inside its circular mask, and because the asset's own
      background is this same butter the mask boundary is invisible: the mark
      lands on an unbroken butter field. The square is 128 dp in all five
      density buckets and the mark occupies its middle ~60%, so nothing is
      clipped — verified, not assumed (silhouette agreement with the source
      asset 98.25%, aspect ratio 1.1237 vs 1.1247).

      Measured on Medium_Phone_API_36.0 (API 36, density 420), light and dark,
      across cold launches: white pixels 172 -> 0, mark 46x51 dp -> 159x179 dp.
      See WP6_FINAL_VERIFICATION_REPORT.md §17.
    -->
    <style name="LaunchTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Light.NoTitleBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@drawable/launch_background</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/bufon_splash</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_isotype</item>
    </style>

    <style name="NormalTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Light.NoTitleBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/bufon_surface</item>
    </style>
</resources>
